 "files": [
  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# VHS Filter\n\nA scene as recovered tape footage: colour smeared sideways off the brightness, the lines wobbling, a head-switch tear along the bottom edge, scanlines and grain. Runs its WebGL shader over its own built-in scene (a stat and a bar chart; label, number and bars from variables), not over the host video.\n\nCategory: filters. Length: 3.0 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A scene should read as recovered tape footage rather than a clean render: retro product spots, 'what we shipped in 2003' beats, lo-fi title cards.\n- You want the whole scene degraded for its full duration, not a one-frame artifact at a cut.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The artifact should live only at the cut between two scenes: use glitch-cut.\n- Only a headline should break up: use rgb-glitch-text.\n- The story is the display or the glass rather than the signal: use crt-screen or camera-lens.\n- You want intermittent digital faults rather than continuous analog wear: use sustained-glitch.\n\nVariables:\n- label (string): Label, default \"Deploys this week\"\n- value (string): Value, default \"2,481\"\n- bars (string): Bars, default \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"\n- accent (color): Highlight, default \"#a1eebd\"\n- bleed (number, 0-3): Bleed, default 1\n- wobble (number, 0-3): Wobble, default 1\n- noise (number, 0-3): Noise, default 1\n- intensity (number, 0-1): Intensity, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  VHS Filter\n\n  A scene held under analog tape: chroma bleed, tape wobble, a head-switch tear and luma\n  noise. The scene here is a stat and a bar chart.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/vhs-filter/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  remocn captures its React children with the HTML-in-Canvas API, which a render machine does\n  not have. This block draws remocn's preview scene (a stat and a bar chart) (text and colours from the variables) on a\n  2D canvas and runs remocn's fragment shader over it, so it applies the look to its own content,\n  not to the host video behind it.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"vhs-filter\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Label\", \"description\": \"Small caption above the number in the sample scene.\", \"default\": \"Deploys this week\"}, {\"id\": \"value\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Value\", \"description\": \"The big number in the sample scene.\", \"default\": \"2,481\"}, {\"id\": \"bars\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Bars\", \"description\": \"Bar heights as percentages, separated by commas (up to 12); the last bar is highlighted.\", \"default\": \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"}, {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Highlight\", \"description\": \"Colour of the last bar.\", \"default\": \"#a1eebd\"}, {\"id\": \"bleed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Bleed\", \"description\": \"How far colour smears sideways.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1}, {\"id\": \"wobble\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Wobble\", \"description\": \"Tape jitter of the lines.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1}, {\"id\": \"noise\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Noise\", \"description\": \"Strength of the grain.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3, \"step\": 0.1}, {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Intensity\", \"description\": \"0 shows the scene, 1 the full tape look.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. The scanlines and grain are fine; lower renders faster but softens them.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>VHS Filter</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .vhs-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .vhs-canvas,\n        .vhs-scene {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .vhs-scene {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .vhs-off .vhs-canvas {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .vhs-off .vhs-fb {\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"vhs-filter\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"vhs-clip\" class=\"vhs-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"vhs-scene0\" class=\"vhs-scene vhs-fb\"></canvas>\n          <canvas id=\"vhs-canvas\" class=\"vhs-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"vhs-filter\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"vhs-clip\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"vhs-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#ffffff\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Deploys this week\"}, {\"id\": \"value\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"2,481\"}, {\"id\": \"bars\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"32,51,43,68,57,86,64,100\"}, {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"default\": \"#a1eebd\"}, {\"id\": \"bleed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3}, {\"id\": \"wobble\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3}, {\"id\": \"noise\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 3}, {\"id\": \"intensity\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 1}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else if (d.type === \"enum\") V[d.id] = d.options.indexOf(raw) >= 0 ? raw : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" && raw.trim() ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var res = V.resolution;\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * res));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * res));\n            var sceneCanvases = [\"vhs-scene0\"].map(function (id) {\n              var el = document.getElementById(id);\n              el.width = cw;\n              el.height = ch;\n              return el;\n            });\n\n            var SANS = \"Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif\";\n            var MONO = \"'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\";\n            var INK = \"#f2f2f2\";\n            var MUTED = \"#8b8f9a\";\n            var TONES = [\"#a1eebd\", \"#ffb38e\", \"#d4b3ff\"];\n            var S = Math.min(W / 940, H / 720);\n            function setFont(ctx, weight, size, family) { ctx.font = weight + \" \" + size + \"px \" + family; }\n            function fitFont(ctx, text, maxWidth, weight, size, family) {\n              setFont(ctx, weight, size, family);\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width;\n              if (w > maxWidth) { size *= maxWidth / w; setFont(ctx, weight, size, family); }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function setSpacing(ctx, px) { if (\"letterSpacing\" in ctx) ctx.letterSpacing = px + \"px\"; }\n            function wrapLines(ctx, text, maxWidth) {\n              var words = String(text).split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n              var lines = [];\n              var line = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (word) {\n                var next = line ? line + \" \" + word : word;\n                if (line && ctx.measureText(next).width > maxWidth) { lines.push(line); line = word; }\n                else line = next;\n              });\n              if (line) lines.push(line);\n              return lines;\n            }\n            function pairs(text, max) {\n              return String(text).split(\";\")\n                .map(function (row) { return row.split(\"|\").map(function (part) { return part.trim(); }); })\n                .filter(function (row) { return row[0]; })\n                .slice(0, max);\n            }\n            function begin(ctx, cw, ch, fill) {\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = fill;\n              ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n              ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n            }\n\n\n            // Sample scene \"A\": a stat and a bar chart (remocn's CanvasSceneA), laid out for any frame size.\n            var barValues = String(V.bars).split(\",\").map(function (n) { return Math.min(100, Math.max(4, Number(n) || 0)); }).slice(0, 12);\n            if (!barValues.length) barValues = [32, 51, 43, 68, 57, 86, 64, 100];\n            function drawA(canvas) {\n              var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n              begin(ctx, canvas.width, canvas.height, \"#0a0a0a\");\n              var s = S, pad = 96 * s, inner = W - pad * 2;\n              var labelH = 41 * s, valueSize = 152 * s, barsH = 190 * s;\n              var total = labelH + 6 * s + valueSize + 52 * s + barsH;\n              var y = (H - total) / 2;\n              ctx.fillStyle = MUTED;\n              fitFont(ctx, V.label, inner, 400, 34 * s, SANS);\n              ctx.fillText(V.label, pad, y + labelH / 2);\n              y += labelH + 6 * s;\n              ctx.fillStyle = INK;\n              setSpacing(ctx, -0.04 * valueSize);\n              fitFont(ctx, V.value, inner, 600, valueSize, SANS);\n              ctx.fillText(V.value, pad, y + valueSize / 2);\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n              y += valueSize + 52 * s;\n              var n = barValues.length;\n              var bs = Math.min(1, inner / ((n * 74 + (n - 1) * 16) * s));\n              var bw = 74 * s * bs, gap = 16 * s * bs, base = y + barsH;\n              barValues.forEach(function (v, i) {\n                var h = barsH * v / 100;\n                ctx.fillStyle = i === n - 1 ? V.accent : \"#23262e\";\n                ctx.beginPath();\n                ctx.roundRect(pad + i * (bw + gap), base - h, bw, h, 10 * s * bs);\n                ctx.fill();\n              });\n            }\n\n            function drawScenes() {\n              drawA(sceneCanvases[0]);\n            }\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  v_uv = vec2(a_pos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - a_pos.y * 0.5);\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\n\nuniform sampler2D u_scene;\nuniform float u_frame;\nuniform float u_time;\nuniform float u_bleed;\nuniform float u_wobble;\nuniform float u_noise;\nuniform float u_intensity;\n\nin vec2 v_uv;\nout vec4 outColor;\n\nconst float PI = 3.141592653589793;\nconst float LINES = 486.0;\nconst int TAPS = 6;\n\nfloat hash(vec2 p) {\n  return fract(sin(dot(p, vec2(127.1, 311.7))) * 43758.5453123);\n}\n\nfloat valueNoise(float x) {\n  float i = floor(x);\n  float f = fract(x);\n  float a = hash(vec2(i, 7.0));\n  float b = hash(vec2(i + 1.0, 7.0));\n  return mix(a, b, f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f));\n}\n\nvec3 rgb2yiq(vec3 c) {\n  return vec3(\n    dot(c, vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114)),\n    dot(c, vec3(0.5959, -0.2746, -0.3213)),\n    dot(c, vec3(0.2115, -0.5227, 0.3112))\n  );\n}\n\nvec3 yiq2rgb(vec3 c) {\n  return vec3(\n    c.x + 0.956 * c.y + 0.619 * c.z,\n    c.x - 0.272 * c.y - 0.647 * c.z,\n    c.x - 1.106 * c.y + 1.703 * c.z\n  );\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  float line = floor(v_uv.y * LINES);\n  float clock = mod(u_frame, 64.0);\n\n  float drift =\n    sin(v_uv.y * 37.0 + u_time * 2.3) * 0.55 +\n    sin(v_uv.y * 96.0 - u_time * 1.1) * 0.25;\n  float jitter = valueNoise(line * 0.61 + u_time * 24.0) - 0.5;\n  float wobble = (drift * 0.35 + jitter * 0.9) * 0.007 * u_wobble * u_intensity;\n\n  float band = smoothstep(0.955, 0.994, v_uv.y);\n  float tear = valueNoise(line * 2.7 + u_time * 43.0) - 0.5;\n  float headSwitch = band * tear * 0.085 * u_intensity;\n\n  vec2 uv = vec2(v_uv.x + wobble + headSwitch, v_uv.y);\n  vec4 base = texture(u_scene, uv);\n  float luma = rgb2yiq(base.rgb).x;\n\n  float smear = u_bleed * 0.02 * u_intensity;\n  vec2 chroma = vec2(0.0);\n  float total = 0.0;\n  for (int i = 0; i < TAPS; i++) {\n    float t = float(i) / float(TAPS - 1);\n    float weight = 1.0 - t * 0.72;\n    vec3 tap = texture(u_scene, vec2(uv.x - smear * t, uv.y)).rgb;\n    chroma += rgb2yiq(tap).yz * weight;\n    total += weight;\n  }\n\n  vec3 color = yiq2rgb(vec3(luma, chroma / total));\n\n  float scan = 0.94 + 0.06 * cos(v_uv.y * LINES * PI);\n  color *= mix(1.0, scan, u_intensity);\n\n  float grain =\n    hash(vec2(v_uv.x * 640.0 + clock * 13.0, line + clock * 5.0)) - 0.5;\n  color += grain * 0.07 * u_noise * u_intensity;\n\n  color = mix(color, vec3(luma), band * 0.55 * u_intensity);\n  color += band * (hash(vec2(line, clock * 3.0)) - 0.5) * 0.26 * u_intensity;\n\n  outColor = vec4(clamp(color, 0.0, 1.0), base.a);\n}`;\n\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            var upload = function () {};\n            var extraUpload = function () {};\n            var frameFn = function () {};\n            var texUnits = [];\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(program);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(program, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(program) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(program);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              function makeTexture(unit) {\n                var texture = gl.createTexture();\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                return texture;\n              }\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program, name); }\n              [\"u_scene\"].forEach(function (name, unit) {\n                makeTexture(unit);\n                gl.uniform1i(u(name), unit);\n              });\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_aspect\"), W / H);\n              var frameLoc = u(\"u_frame\");\n              var timeLoc = u(\"u_time\");\n              upload = function () {\n                sceneCanvases.forEach(function (el, unit) {\n                  gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                  gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, el);\n                });\n                extraUpload();\n              };\n\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_bleed\"), V.bleed);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_wobble\"), V.wobble);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_noise\"), V.noise);\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_intensity\"), V.intensity);\n\n              paint = function (frame) {\n                gl.uniform1f(frameLoc, frame);\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, frame / 30);\n                frameFn(frame, frame / 30);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              stage.classList.add(\"vhs-off\");\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            // The scenes are redrawn whenever a web font finishes loading, so no frame keeps a fallback face.\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            var sceneEpoch = -1;\n            var lastFrame = 0;\n            function render(frame) {\n              lastFrame = frame;\n              if (sceneEpoch !== fontEpoch) {\n                sceneEpoch = fontEpoch;\n                drawScenes();\n                upload();\n              }\n              if (paint) paint(frame);\n            }\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"400 34px Geist\", \"500 30px Geist\", \"600 44px Geist\", \"400 44px 'Geist Mono'\"].forEach(function (face) {\n                document.fonts.load(face).then(function () { fontEpoch++; render(lastFrame); }, function () {});\n              });\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, {\n              frame: totalFrames,\n              duration: total,\n              ease: \"none\",\n              onUpdate: function () { render(Math.round(clock.frame)); }\n            }, 0);\n            render(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
